Seascape by Alexander Alekseev aka TDM (2014)
Original: https://www.shadertoy.com/view/Ms2SD1

The author's notice in the shader's own header reads:

    "License Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 3.0 Unported License."

It appears in the comment block at the top of Seascape.frag (the author's header,
"Seascape by Alexander Alekseev aka TDM - 2014", with the contact tdmaav@gmail.com), as
published at
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/y4my4my4m/kde-shader-wallpaper/HEAD/package/contents/ui/Shaders/Seascape.frag
That repository's own GPL-3.0 licence does not cover this shader; the author's statement
above is the one relied on. The same statement, credited to the same author and to
https://www.shadertoy.com/view/Ms2SD1, also appears in other independent copies of the
code. (The Shadertoy page itself could not be read automatically.) The author's header
is kept unchanged at the top of main.metal.

Ported to Metal Shading Language for MacOS Live Wallpaper. What was changed:
  - mainImage's and heightMapTracing's output parameters are declared as thread
    references (Metal has no `out`).
  - Two local variables that Metal does not zero (`p` in getPixel, `d` in map and
    map_detailed) start at zero.
  - The mouse term in `time` is removed (iMouse is always zero in a wallpaper).
  - The horizon blend smoothstep(0.0, -0.02, y) is written as
    1.0 - smoothstep(-0.02, 0.0, y): the same curve, without reversed edges, which
    Metal leaves undefined.
  - A ray that points at or above the horizon returns the sky colour straight away.
    Its sea weight is exactly zero there and the camera is above every wave, so the
    picture is the same; it only skips the trace.
  - The camera (its turn, sway and forward drift) runs at 0.3 of the original speed
    (LW_PACE), so the scene suits a desktop background. As written, the view swings
    through a full turn every 21 seconds. The waves' own motion, the lighting, the
    colours and every constant of the sea are unchanged.
  - The author's optional 3x3 supersampling switch (#define AA) is turned off.
No textures are used and none are shipped.

